  "claims": [
    "Typed Slot references and universal symbolic inputs work for arbitrary atomic sorts and product/unit shapes. A wire normal layout is a finite output-shaped tuple of input references retaining all atom types.",
    "normal_complete characterizes equality of these layouts by equality of wire evaluation for EVERY value family and input. This adds no semantic-equality rewrite generator. The equational normalization proof does not require decidable equality of atomic sorts.",
    "The existing Wire syntax has an explicit eighteen-form cartesian root-equation presentation, with composition/tensor congruence, symmetry and transitivity. Projections and pairing are fixed Wire macros, not new opaque boxes or whole-normalization roots.",
    "normalize recursively constructs a Cell from every wire to a reified layout using only those roots. normalize_layout identifies the computed layout with symbolic evaluation; reify_normal and canonical_idempotent prove canonical layout reconstruction and idempotence.",
    "complete proves FIRST-LEVEL equational completeness on the original typed Wire syntax: a Cartesian.Cell exists exactly when evaluations agree for every atomic value family and input. connect constructs a witness from equal layouts.",
    "With decidable equality of atom names, equivalent decides universal pure-wire equality and certify returns a derived Cell exactly when one exists. Cell.toTrack compiles derived cells into actual eighteen-root contextual rewrite proof tracks.",
    "The old eleven-root reversible language preserves leftUnitInvCount, so left-unit inverse cancellation cannot be derived there for any shape. The new presentation derives it; fromOldRoot also constructs new derivations for each old root.",
    "Unrestricted forward application of the eighteen roots is NOT terminating: copy expansion creates an infinite contextual copy chain, formally refuting well-foundedness. This does not contradict termination of the structural recursive normalization algorithm or idempotence of its representative.",
    "A generic pure-wiring rewrite catalogue embeds these proof tracks into mixed circuits with arbitrary opaque probabilistic boxes. Structural normalization support is empty; a single mixed placement adds exactly its fixed-context needs.",
    "normalized_repaired_joint compares the updated kernels while retaining correlated prior data and input, using only cached/transferred/rechecked context conditions. The concrete MAC instantiation and mac_repaired_joint retain the existing full state/trace and indexed conditions.",
    "Actual MAC tensor contexts followed by output copy or discard have support exactly {stage} for every stage. The pure normalization contributes no additional condition IDs."
  ],
