  "limits": [
    "Completeness is first-level pure cartesian equational completeness, not higher coherence between proof paths, a finite mixed homotopy basis, or an exhaustive critical-diagram classifier.",
    "The eighteen forms are parameterized local equation patterns. They are not a finite list of all ground typed cells. No arbitrary semantic-equality or whole-normalization root is used.",
    "Canonical layout/reified-representative normalization is not irreducibility under all directed roots. Unrestricted directed termination is explicitly false, so a convergent-rewriting coherence theorem cannot be applied to these orientations without additional work.",
    "The generic mixed catalogue contains only the new pure structural rules. It is usable inside fixed probabilistic contexts, but has not been merged with all previous MAC/fusion rules or supplied with a complete higher basis for that union.",
    "The generic joint repair theorem takes one Placement layer. Repeated placements construct nested certificates; the concrete MAC copy/discard examples verify a nested case. No new all-context higher coherence theorem is inferred.",
    "Universal equality across all value families/inputs is stronger than equality for one concrete type, a constrained reachable-state invariant or a particular correlated input law. This is not a decision procedure for arbitrary cryptographic program equivalence.",
    "The cartesian laws apply to deterministic routing on already obtained values. They neither commute duplication through arbitrary probabilistic boxes nor clone mutable oracle executions. Internal pure computations may be duplicated or erased in equational proofs; actual runtime/resource equality is not established.",
    "Empty structural guard support and indexed guard counts are not measured verification cost or a proof of minimal security assumptions. Joint repair is within the updated model, not equality of old and updated model distributions.",
    "No total certificate size/checking-time bound, equal-information ordinary-proof separation, new security bound, computational reduction implementation or continuing native-machine contract is supplied."
  ],
